<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
	The hold, the second half of an inspection.

	TienInspectWeapon.xml is the wind-up: the character brings the weapon up to look at it,
	and when that finishes the window opens and this node takes over for as long
	as the player is reading. Two nodes rather than one because the two halves are doing
	different things - one is an action with a duration, the other is a pose being held -
	and because a single clip stretched across both reads as a loop nobody chose.

	The clip is the mod's own, Bob_TienInspect_1H_Hold (built by scripts/anim/clips/inspect.py):
	an 8 second loop of looking the weapon over - turn it to one side and pause, to the other
	and pause, then along the edge, and back - with the head following it. Like the raise,
	this is the one-handed clip and the fallback; the _2H, _Handgun and _Rifle variants
	take over by the Weapon variable.

	The hold can run for the whole sandbox ceiling, so it has to survive looping: each hold
	clip's last frame leads back into its first by less than an ordinary frame's step.

	m_Looped is true here and false everywhere in vanilla's actions folder, because every
	vanilla action is short enough to finish. This one is not, and the game's own idle, walk
	and run nodes are the precedent for a node that has to keep going.

	No m_SubStateBoneWeights, for the same reason TienInspectWeapon.xml has none - see the
	comment there.

	Persistent mode (InspectMode 2) plays this node too, as the whole of its one timed action
	(ISTienInspectWeaponPersistentAction): the studying pose for the raise time, then the
	window opens and the character is free again.
-->
<animNode>
	<m_Name>TienInspectWeaponHold</m_Name>
	<m_AnimName>Bob_TienInspect_1H_Hold</m_AnimName>
	<m_Looped>true</m_Looped>
	<m_BlendTime>0.30</m_BlendTime>
	<m_SpeedScale>1.0</m_SpeedScale>
	<m_SyncTrackingEnabled>false</m_SyncTrackingEnabled>
	<m_Conditions x_name="3e59b7c4-8a12-4f6d-b0e7-2c9d41f8a6b3">
		<m_Name>PerformingAction</m_Name>
		<m_Type>STRING</m_Type>
		<m_Value>TienInspectWeaponHold</m_Value>
	</m_Conditions>
</animNode>
